Intersection of Two Arrays
Exercise

Given two integer arrays, return their unique intersection.

The order of the result does not matter.

Example:

nums1 = [1, 2, 2, 1]
nums2 = [2, 2]

Output: [2]
nums1 = [4, 9, 5]
nums2 = [9, 4, 9, 8, 4]

Output: [4, 9]



Solution:


nums1 = [4, 9, 5];
nums2 = [9, 4, 9, 8, 4];
let set = new Set(nums1);
let set2 = new Set(nums2);

const output = [];

for (let num of set) {
  if (set2.has(num)) {
    output.push(num);
  }
}

console.log(output);
